# Liaison IDE hop — tab goal release

**Invariant:** `liaison_ide_hop.ok ∧ departing_attended_tab ⇒ UpdateGoal(complete)` same turn — **before**
the `RETIRED → <transcript_id>` line. Harness `retire_departing_tab` cannot do this (Cursor-native).

| Meaning | `UpdateGoal(complete)` on hop? |
|---|---|
| House arc / scoreboard fully closed | Yes (arc close) |
| Hop landed; house still open on bus | **Yes (tab-goal release)** |
| Loop stopped; no hop | Only if objective met; else leave active |

**Tool (verbatim):** `CallDynamicTool(namespace="cursor", toolName="UpdateGoal", arguments={"status":"complete"})`.

**Script cues:** `liaison-ide-hop.py` JSON field `goal_release`; stderr `LIAISON_HOP_TAB_GOAL_RELEASE` (see
`libs/bus_watch/ide_hop_retire.GOAL_RELEASE`).

**Successor:** `CreateGoal` with same house objective from tip CHECKPOINT (liaison skill step 0).

**Anti-pattern:** Refusing `complete` because Gate-1 / scoreboard rows remain open — that blocks tab retire
and re-injects the goal on the departing tab (11912, 12088 2026-09-21).

Playbook: Use the `liaison` skill § Hop step 2 · command `.cursor/commands/liaison.md` Hop section.
